    "name": "Python 3 code to rotate an array",
    "code": "# Python 3 code to rotate an array\n# and answer the index query\n \n# Function to compute the element\n# at given index\ndef findElement(arr, ranges, rotations, index) :\n     \n    for i in range(rotations - 1, -1, -1 ) :\n     \n        # Range[left...right]\n        left = ranges[i][0]\n        right = ranges[i][1]\n \n        # Rotation will not have\n        # any effect\n        if (left <= index and right >= index) :\n            if (index == left) :\n                index = right\n            else :\n                index = index - 1\n         \n    # Returning new element\n    return arr[index]\n \n# Driver Code\narr = [ 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 ]\n \n# No. of rotations\nrotations = 2\n \n# Ranges according to\n# 0-based indexing\nranges = [ [ 0, 2 ], [ 0, 3 ] ]\n \nindex = 1\n \nprint(findElement(arr, ranges, rotations, index))\n     \n# This code is contributed by Nikita Tiwari.",
